# ALL.mask -- CEO-409 line masks for the dotnet suite, declared beside the data (the coo 2026-09-28, ceo CEO-1344: a SPITBOL fatal is
# gradable). This suite is graded by live oracle diff and carries no .ref; test_snobol4_dotnet_suite.sh applies these rows to BOTH
# streams through util_apply_ceo409_mask.py (the harness's own reader) for every program (CEO-1352, hq_snobol4: the -LIST listing
# rows of SourceLines001-003 below); the five `*` rows match only a fatal block's run summary (1brc.sno, asgn1.sno today). The five lines are the oracle's run summary after the fatal -- engine
# bookkeeping, not the program's answer -- and SCRIP's rendered block prints each with a dash where it carries no figure, so the
# placeholder lands on both sides. FORMAT: entry<TAB>python-regex<TAB>reason.
*	^stmts executed       ([0-9]+|-)$	CEO-1344 (a SPITBOL fatal is gradable, the coo 2026-09-28): SPITBOL's own statement counter, printed in its fatal block -- oracle-internal until SCRIP reports its own count; SCRIP's rendered block carries a dash.
*	^execution time msec  ([0-9]+|-)$	CEO-1344: SPITBOL's own clock reading in its fatal block, a duration and never a program's answer; SCRIP's rendered block carries a dash.
*	^REGENERATIONS        ([0-9]+|-)$	CEO-1344: SPITBOL's own collector count in its fatal block, engine bookkeeping and not the program's data; SCRIP's rendered block carries a dash.
*	^memory used \(bytes\)  ([0-9]+|-)$	SPITBOL's own allocator arithmetic (CEO-420 clause (b), the csnobol4 ALL.mask demonstration: two programs with byte-identical output read different figures), printed in every fatal block (CEO-1344); SCRIP's rendered block carries a dash.
*	^memory left \(bytes\)  ([0-9]+|-)$	The same allocator arithmetic from the other side, masked with its twin or not at all (CEO-1344); SCRIP's rendered block carries a dash.
SourceLines001	^(macro spitbol|snobol4dotnet|snobol4jvm) version [0-9][0-9.a-z]*$	CEO-1344 ORACLE-IDENTITY (CEO-1352, the ceo 2026-09-28: the -LIST listing's version line takes an identity mask; CEO-1858 item 4 and CEO-1864 (6)(b): snobol4dotnet keeps its own name on that line, so the mask admits it): a -LIST listing head names the engine's own build, never the program's answer. CEO-1907 (the ceo 2026-10-22, on hq_jvm's ask): snobol4jvm keeps its own name on that line too, "snobol4jvm version 0.2.0", so the mask admits it.
SourceLines001	^x86-64  [A-Z][a-z][a-z] [A-Z][a-z][a-z] [ 0-9][0-9] [0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9] [0-9]{4}$	CEO-409 CLOCK (CEO-1352: the -LIST listing's date-time line takes a clock mask): the wall-clock time the listing was printed.
SourceLines002	^(macro spitbol|snobol4dotnet|snobol4jvm) version [0-9][0-9.a-z]*$	CEO-1344 ORACLE-IDENTITY (CEO-1352, the ceo 2026-09-28: the -LIST listing's version line takes an identity mask; CEO-1858 item 4 and CEO-1864 (6)(b): snobol4dotnet keeps its own name on that line, so the mask admits it): a -LIST listing head names the engine's own build, never the program's answer. CEO-1907 (the ceo 2026-10-22, on hq_jvm's ask): snobol4jvm keeps its own name on that line too, "snobol4jvm version 0.2.0", so the mask admits it.
SourceLines002	^x86-64  [A-Z][a-z][a-z] [A-Z][a-z][a-z] [ 0-9][0-9] [0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9] [0-9]{4}$	CEO-409 CLOCK (CEO-1352: the -LIST listing's date-time line takes a clock mask): the wall-clock time the listing was printed.
SourceLines003	^(macro spitbol|snobol4dotnet|snobol4jvm) version [0-9][0-9.a-z]*$	CEO-1344 ORACLE-IDENTITY (CEO-1352, the ceo 2026-09-28: the -LIST listing's version line takes an identity mask; CEO-1858 item 4 and CEO-1864 (6)(b): snobol4dotnet keeps its own name on that line, so the mask admits it): a -LIST listing head names the engine's own build, never the program's answer. CEO-1907 (the ceo 2026-10-22, on hq_jvm's ask): snobol4jvm keeps its own name on that line too, "snobol4jvm version 0.2.0", so the mask admits it.
SourceLines003	^x86-64  [A-Z][a-z][a-z] [A-Z][a-z][a-z] [ 0-9][0-9] [0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9] [0-9]{4}$	CEO-409 CLOCK (CEO-1352: the -LIST listing's date-time line takes a clock mask): the wall-clock time the listing was printed.
*	^(macro spitbol|snobol4dotnet|snobol4jvm) version [0-9][0-9.a-z]*$	the head of a listing page names the engine that printed it (a compile refusal prints one); each engine keeps its own name (CEO-1859), so the line is masked for every entry, as SourceLines001 to 003 already were (seat dotnet 2026-11-19, the TestSnobol4 move)
*	^x86-64  [A-Z][a-z][a-z] [A-Z][a-z][a-z] [ 0-9][0-9] [0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9] [0-9]{4}$	the head of a listing page carries the clock, never equal on two runs; masked for every entry (seat dotnet 2026-11-19)
Collect__TEST_Collect_002_returns_integer	^c = [0-9]+$	the COLLECT ruling of 2026-11-13 (skill snobol4 section 7): COLLECT() answers the free storage, a figure of the implementation, never faked, masked in both streams; MEASURED 2026-11-21 on snobol4dotnet 53995cc against the ref (sbl -bf -D1): c = 129541 under sbl, 16755405 under snobol4dotnet; every other line of the dump equal (seat dotnet)
Collect__TEST_Collect_005_returns_nonneg	^c[12] = [0-9]+$	the COLLECT ruling of 2026-11-13 (skill snobol4 section 7): COLLECT() answers the free storage, a figure of the implementation, never faked, masked in both streams; MEASURED 2026-11-21 on snobol4dotnet 53995cc against the ref (sbl -bf -D1): c1 and c2 read 129523 and 129530 under sbl, 16754760 and 16754729 under snobol4dotnet; every other line equal (seat dotnet)
Collect__TEST_Collect_answers_the_same_storage_twice_with_nothing_between	^(NOW|PREV) = [0-9]+$	the COLLECT ruling of 2026-11-13 (skill snobol4 section 7): COLLECT() answers the free storage, a figure of the implementation, never faked, masked in both streams; MEASURED 2026-11-21 on snobol4dotnet 53995cc against the ref (sbl -bf -D1): NOW and PREV, the last COLLECT() read, 129439 under sbl, 16751093 under snobol4dotnet (seat dotnet)
Collect__TEST_Collect_answers_the_same_storage_twice_with_nothing_between	^D = -?[0-9]+$	the COLLECT ruling of 2026-11-13 (skill snobol4 section 7): COLLECT() answers the free storage, a figure of the implementation, never faked, masked in both streams; MEASURED 2026-11-21 on snobol4dotnet 53995cc against the ref (sbl -bf -D1): D, the last difference of two COLLECT() readings (seat dotnet)
Collect__TEST_Collect_answers_the_same_storage_twice_with_nothing_between	^DIFFS = '[- 0-9]*$	the COLLECT ruling of 2026-11-13 (skill snobol4 section 7): COLLECT() answers the free storage, a figure of the implementation, never faked, masked in both streams; MEASURED 2026-11-21 on snobol4dotnet 53995cc against the ref (sbl -bf -D1): the first line of DIFFS, the differences of successive COLLECT() readings, 0 -3 -2 0 1 ... under sbl, 0 -7 0 -1 -1 ... under snobol4dotnet, each two lines long; SWINGS, the program's answer (no difference past 128), reads 0 under both (seat dotnet)
Collect__TEST_Collect_answers_the_same_storage_twice_with_nothing_between	^[- 0-9]*'$	the COLLECT ruling of 2026-11-13 (skill snobol4 section 7): COLLECT() answers the free storage, a figure of the implementation, never faked, masked in both streams; MEASURED 2026-11-21 on snobol4dotnet 53995cc against the ref (sbl -bf -D1): the second line of DIFFS, the dump's wrap of the same figures at the page width (seat dotnet)
Collect__TEST_Collect_sees_the_storage_of_a_released_array_as_freed	^(FREED|HELD) = [0-9]+$	the COLLECT ruling of 2026-11-13 (skill snobol4 section 7): COLLECT() answers the free storage, a figure of the implementation, never faked, masked in both streams; MEASURED 2026-11-21 on snobol4dotnet 53995cc against the ref (sbl -bf -D1): HELD 126504 and FREED 3001 under sbl, 16750868 and 3083 under snobol4dotnet: each engine's own storage units; I equal (seat dotnet)
HostIdentity__TEST_HostIdentity_has_three_fields_none_empty	^H = '[^:]+:[^:]+:.+'$	CEO-1344 oracle identity, masked by its three-field shape as test/host is (the coo's ruling of 2026-11-15, skill snobol4 section 7): HOST() with no argument answers the implementation's own host string, x86-64:unix :Macro SPITBOL 15.01 # under sbl -bf, x86-64:Unix 7.0.0.43:SNOBOL4.net Version 0.1 # under snobol4dotnet (MEASURED 2026-11-21, seat dotnet)
